{"title":"GATE 2027-Topicwise Test-2 (Electric Circuits -2)","fileName":"042_GATE 2027-Topicwise Test-2 (Electric Circuits -2).html","branch":"ELECTRICAL ENGINEERING","series":"GATE 2027 Online Test Series - Electrical Engineering","provider":"MADE EASY","duration":2700,"questions":[{"qnum":1,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>In the following figure is shown a network in which a steady state is reached with switch K open.<br />At <em>t </em>= 0, the switch is closed. For the element given,</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/7180764b0e21a93c1763a60bfb6437da33559f8b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>The value of V<sub>a</sub>(0<sup>&ndash;</sup>) and V<sub>a</sub>(0<sup>+</sup>) are respectively:</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>5 V and 3 V respectively</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>2 V and 3 V respectively</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>3 V and 5 V respectively</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>2 V and 5 V respectively</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/d35634966e344aeae982a138112b0e9632d46664.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +2 / -0.66"},{"qnum":2,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider the following circuit:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/477cf5beeed2710ec5e75e35f16c1da07f39aef6.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>The resonant frequency of the circuit is _________ rad/sec.</p></div>\n<div><span>Numerical answer type</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"0.5","high":"0.5"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/dfc0dd90e31165b02b01e174957e9937a8177d75.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/2c9cecf5294098fc19ff48455810516432a70c4c.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"numerical | Marks +2"},{"qnum":3,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Three identical resistance are connected in a star fashion against a balanced three phase voltage supply. If one of the resistances be removed then the percentage reduction in power is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>17.32%</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>33.33%</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>14.14%</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>50%</p></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/3c582f5af2949050e15e0359c33cb709de2ae1bf.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +1 / -0.33"},{"qnum":4,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>A series circuit consists of 2 &Omega; resistor, 0.01 H inductor and a capacitor &lsquo;<em>C</em>&rsquo; across 200-V mains.<br />Assume the above series circuit resonates at 50 Hz frequency, then the value of voltage across capacitor &lsquo;<em>C</em>&rsquo; at resonance is (in magnitude) _________ V. (upto two decimal places)</p></div>\n<div><span>Numerical answer type</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"312","high":"316"},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/5581f2bc827dbac9277a824cbeec10a5d5829fcb.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"numerical | Marks +2"},{"qnum":5,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":2,"wrong":0.66,"qtext":"<p>For the below given network,</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/0c59f6db0e9c80f9c57e652a9c319aedb939b363.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>Which of the following is correct?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>Network is symmetrical but not reciprocal.</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>Network is not symmetrical but reciprocal</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>Network is not symmetrical and not reciprocal</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>Network is symmetrical as well as reciprocal.</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/55e34c69e048201166a55125c9c8bf2da15ec721.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=