":"B","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/b41d06eb6ab0fd5d232dfb55962f0cf85314a725.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/51213c046ea453d8ac55c4649580dc1260071c80.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/16513a1d385dcc031b4fa5a5b118eab77c5dd731.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/95b2a326191767fb4a0382d4221a39bcec258190.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/529ce20e46b5e4e6ad0cc1d535f26ef0cab433d2.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +1 / -0.33"},{"qnum":13,"type":"MSQ","correct":"C,A,B,D","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider the circuit shown below:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/1394bb6ebd2694d9979fdd7b49907a2a6369f0eb.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>The inductors and capacitors do not contain any stored energy. If the switch is closed at time <em>t </em>= 0, then which of the following options is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>Voltage across 6 H inductor is 150 V at <em>t </em>= 0<sup>+</sup>.</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>Voltage across 8 H inductor is 75 V at <em>t</em> = 0<sup>+</sup>.</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>Voltage across 4 F capacitor is 85.71 V at <em>t</em> = &infin;.</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>Voltage across 5 F capacitor is 142.85 V at <em>t</em> = &infin;.</p></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/26d8b3e900ac39cf9fd0019bacb84744b759d435.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"multi | Marks +2"},{"qnum":14,"type":"MCQ","correct":"C","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>For the circuit shown below, if <em>i </em>= 8 cos 500<em>t</em> A in the network, the total energy stored in the network is &lsquo;<em>x&rsquo;</em> Joules.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/0c71ebd7df902732fe2823acd80ef324e6704b02.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>For storing same amount of energy, the circuit we can use is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/3c0c9eeab0575411258f467372e29f6dbb01025a.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/111f503503f33192c583824de4c9bb5e00c4ceee.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/3fc0e9f8dffdeeb0715381f8cb4bfe3d72bc9a5b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/3795cda7e24b81685eb401a246fa4cf8d7d5bf72.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/be1d2ee1fe4c4cb37bd2ffe6946129c9ec89c878.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +1 / -0.33"},{"qnum":15,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>For the circuit shown, the switch is closes at <em>t </em>= 0 (after having been open for a very long time).<br />The current <em>i</em>(<em>t</em>) is given by (for <em>t </em>&ge; 0):</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/52256b960eb898abbe2450d2581df03fdfc6b601.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/f3f308922f22e97b1f13051b48f9ef3f64615c01.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/c420f3a0b05827b348fcb012ba939fd3ecf59f48.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/3fd2bb7c29422140fbd5561be575f2f8d9eea9d5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/b267ff8cdb91dc506e2d5de371053ba3a1f5dd68.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>Since the switch was open for a long time, the capacitor was initially discharged. After the switch is closed, the capacitor looks initially like a short circuit thus drawing a current of 1 mA. As time progresses the capacitor charges and thus approaches an open circuit so that <em>i</em>(&infin;) = 0. <br />The RC time constant is obtained from the two 20 k&Omega; resistors in parallel and the 10 &mu;F capacitor, or RC = 10<sup>&ndash;1</sup> sec.</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/c76566e3380999e8af79631fcf26be3ea3789b99.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +1 / -0.33"},{"qnum":16,"type":"MSQ","correct":"B,D","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider the given circuit:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/a6b709967ac5805329b643499c46965816b7c268.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>If the circuit is intitially relaxed, then which of the following option(s) is/are correct?</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/cc9d19b83b82425edd4f48535497b8473db7a00b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/73147c4d2d55b3758f871516ff9ec26503b89bb5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/a76ebcfd458ac7155de1dee7f020462083f9e033.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p><img src=\"/media/85c881ad38feedd956a9a2d2dc7a298da4a36038.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p><img src=\"/media/ba06c38a4b025c065822fcebaa5c8f9224c6073e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/b5b6d59513e8e481f437ecfa0971dcefb50333db.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"multi | Marks +1"},{"qnum":17,"type":"MCQ","correct":"A","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Consider the following circuit:</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/4911c0e123017cf0779a92911992c92e2b58568b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>\n<p>If switch <em>S </em>is closed at <em>t </em>= 0, then current &lsquo;<em>i</em>&rsquo; through the battery at <em>t </em>= 0<sup>+</sup> and <em>t</em> = &infin; are respectively:</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div><p>4.5 A and 4.5 A</p></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div><p>4.5 A and 0 A</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div><p>0 A and 4.5 A</p></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div><p>2.5 A and 4.5 A</p></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>At <em>t </em>= 0<sup>+</sup>, inductor is open but capacitor is shorted and at t = infinity capacitor is open inductor is shorted.<br />So, at both times</p>\n<p><img src=\"/media/ade114457a62964e69238255433ad72dddfe462f.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></p>","subject":"single | Marks +1 / -0.33"}],"questionCount":17,"parsedAt":"2026-11-10T19:39:09.245Z"}